<title>NETHERLANDS: Krasnapolsky buys South African hotel.</title>
<headline>Krasnapolsky buys South African hotel.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch hotel and restaurant chain Krasnapolsky NV said on Thursday it had agreed to buy hotel 'The Lord Charles' in Cape Town, South Africa.</p>
<p>The five-star hotel has 200 rooms and permission to build another 100. It is situated at 25 minutes' distance from Cape Town's central business district and 15 minutes from the international airport, Krasnapolsky said.</p>
<p>It added that tourism in the Cape Town area is growing by more than 20 percent per year.</p>
<p>The takeover is expected to contribute positively to 1997 profits, Krasnapolsky said.</p>
